        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8ab11e46-2540-5866-8d67-ec40bed46461",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Dustin Archbold, John D. Rockefeller\n- Companies: Standard Oil Company\n- Places: Archbold Gymnasium, Archbold Stadium, Carrier Dome, Manley Field House\n- Organizations: Syracuse University\n\nFacts:\n- John Dustin Archbold's small oil company was bought by John D. Rockefeller's Standard Oil Company.\n- Archbold Gymnasium was built in 1908 with money donated by John Dustin Archbold for Syracuse University.\n- John Dustin Archbold was a major benefactor of Syracuse University and also funded Archbold Stadium west of Archbold Gymnasium.\n- The Carrier Dome now stands on the site of Archbold Stadium.\n- Archbold Gymnasium served for almost 60 years before Manley Field House was built to replace it.",
